Eliminate duplicated types in web-ui by importing from shared schema
────────────────────────────────────────
ULID:      01KJ4F7XFGJVY44SC1KA0FQMAD
Slugs:     task-deduplicate-web-ui-types
Type:      task
Status:    pending_review
Priority:  3
Automation: eligible

─── Description ───
  packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/triage.ts manually mirrors types from src/schema/triage.ts. If the schema changes, web-ui types silently diverge. The codebase has @kynetic-ai/shared for shared types (already imported in api.ts), but triage types bypass this. Scope: 1) Audit all packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/ files for types that duplicate src/schema/ definitions. 2) For each duplicated type, determine if it can be imported from the shared package or needs a re-export. 3) Migrate triage types and any other duplicates to use the shared source of truth. 4) Add a lint rule or CI check to prevent future type duplication.
Tags:      refactor, web-ui, types
Created:   2026-02-23T05:23:35.534Z
Started:   2026-02-23T13:05:20.590Z

─── Notes ───
[2026-02-23T08:51:58.014Z] @claude:
AUTOMATION: Standalone refactor. Audit packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/ for duplicated src/schema/ types. Import from @kynetic-ai/shared instead.
[2026-02-23T13:17:01.321Z] @claude:
Audited packages/web-ui/src/lib/types/ and found 4 clear duplicates (TriageStatus, TriageAction, TriageRecord, Convention) plus 5 types (ExportedTask, ExportedItem, InheritedAC, ExportedValidation, KspecSnapshot) duplicated from src/export/types.ts. Added all missing types to @kynetic-ai/shared api.ts. Replaced both web-ui types files with re-exports from shared. Added static analysis test (web-ui-shared-types.test.ts) that enforces no local interface/type definitions in the types directory. Updated existing web-ui-triage.test.ts to verify re-export pattern. All 3196 tests pass.
